---
/**
 * The Prose sample: a short case study with every element Prose styles.
 * `headingTag` is the level of its first heading; the next one is one lower,
 * so the sample fits under the heading of the page it sits on.
 */
import Prose from "../../components/Prose.astro";

interface Props {
	headingTag?: "h2" | "h3" | "h4";
}

const { headingTag: Heading = "h2" } = Astro.props;
const Sub = Heading === "h2" ? "h3" : Heading === "h3" ? "h4" : "h5";
---

<Prose>
	<p>
		Northwind moves fresh food across the Midwest with a fleet of 140 trucks. Their old brand was built for a
		company a tenth of the size, and their site was a <a href="#pdf">PDF brochure</a> with a contact form.
	</p>
	<Heading>What we changed</Heading>
	<p>We started with the trailers, because that is where most people meet the brand. Then we worked inward:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>A wordmark that reads at highway speed.</li>
		<li>A two-color system that survives road grime and cheap vinyl.</li>
		<li>A site with <strong>one job</strong>: get a quote request in under a minute.</li>
	</ul>
	<Sub>Planning the rollout</Sub>
	<ol>
		<li>Trailers at the yearly service.</li>
		<li>Uniforms with the spring order.</li>
		<li>The website on March 1.</li>
	</ol>
	<blockquote><p>We could finally send people to our site without apologizing first.</p></blockquote>
	<p>The quote form posts to their dispatch system with a plain <code>fetch()</code> call:</p>
	<pre><code>await fetch("/api/quote", &#123; method: "POST", body: form &#125;);</code></pre>
	<hr />
	<table>
		<thead><tr><th>Page</th><th>Before</th><th>After</th></tr></thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr><td>Home</td><td>4.8s</td><td>1.1s</td></tr>
			<tr><td>Quote</td><td>6.2s</td><td>1.2s</td></tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>
</Prose>
